==============================================================================
PART 2.  Saturation of Lam in an even unimodular ambient lattice
==============================================================================
   combination     square (mod 4)   reason it cannot be 2y
   e                 0 (mod 4 = 0)    y^2 = 0 needs primitivity of e (fibration lemma)
   f                 0 (mod 4 = 0)    y^2 = 0 needs primitivity of f (fibration lemma)
   E                -2 (mod 4 = 2)    y^2 = -1/2, not integral
   e+f               4 (mod 4 = 0)    y^2 = 1, odd
   e+E              -2 (mod 4 = 2)    y^2 = -1/2, not integral
   f+E              -2 (mod 4 = 2)    y^2 = -1/2, not integral
   e+f+E             2 (mod 4 = 2)    y^2 = 1/2, not integral
   => {e,f,E} is F_2-independent in L/2L  =>  Lam cap 2L = 2Lam
   => every S with Lam <= S <= L equals Lam (as S subset Lam^v, 2S subset Lam)

   model L_K3 = U^3+E8(-1)^2: rank 22, det -1, sig (3, 19), even True
   e^2 = 0, f^2 = 0, 2(e.f) = 4, E^2 = -2
   model: e       lies in 2L_K3? False
   model: f       lies in 2L_K3? False
   model: E       lies in 2L_K3? False
   model: e+f     lies in 2L_K3? False
   model: e+E     lies in 2L_K3? False
   model: f+E     lies in 2L_K3? False
   model: e+f+E   lies in 2L_K3? False

