PART 4.  Construction side: Lefschetz ranks and the joint rank system
==============================================================================
   k=0: chi(Fix I_dP) = -16 -> rk S_dP = 2 (= k+2 = 2)
   k=0: chi(Fix I_Co) = 0  -> rk S_Co = 10 (= k+10 = 10)
   k=1: chi(Fix I_dP) = -14 -> rk S_dP = 3 (= k+2 = 3)
   k=1: chi(Fix I_Co) = 2  -> rk S_Co = 11 (= k+10 = 11)
   J symplectic with 8 fixed points: chi = 8 -> rk S_J = 14
   construction k=1  (rk S_Co, rk S_dP, rk S_J) = (11, 3, 14) -> (a_++,a_+-,a_-+,a_--,) = (3, 8, 0, 11)
   twist             (rk S_Co, rk S_dP, rk S_J) = (11, 10, 21) -> (a_++,a_+-,a_-+,a_--,) = (10, 1, 0, 11)
   the two quadruples differ => no O(L_K3)-isometry carries one G-action to the other
   construction side: a_-+ = 0 <=> S_dP subset S_Co <=> S_dP = Lam (as Lam <= S_Co)

